Produce the declared output set: glTF, ortho views, sidecar

Spec §8.3 names five artefacts and the server was storing only what a backend
happened to emit. It now derives the rest.

- glTF 2.0 binary delivery mesh, written without a dependency and checked in
  tests with pygltflib, an independent parser. Writing a format and reading it
  back with your own reader proves only that you are self-consistent. Point
  clouds are written with mode POINTS so a reconstruction that recovered no
  surface looks like a point cloud rather than a mesh that failed to render.

- Six orthographic views. Determinism is the requirement, not beauty: these
  feed the perceptual mesh hash in phase 5, so the projection is fixed, faces
  are drawn in a total order, and shading comes from geometry alone. A test
  renders the same mesh twice and requires byte-identical PNGs, and a second
  test checks they are not six blank pages — a renderer that silently produced
  nothing would pass the hash test.

- A sidecar record carrying the rubric identity and the capture class beside
  the final one. A record showing only the final class cannot be audited:
  nobody can tell whether reconstruction confirmed the capture estimate or
  contradicted it, which is the most interesting thing about it.

E57 is NOT produced. The spec asks for it, but writing its XML-plus-
CompressedVector structure without libE57Format risks a file that opens in one
program and fails in the one a conservator uses. Every record declares it under
notProduced with the reason rather than leaving it quietly missing.

Two bugs found by running it:

- The PLY list-property header "property list uchar int vertex_index" was
  unpacked in the wrong order, so the index type read as "vertex_index" and
  every binary PLY with faces failed.

- finished_at was stamped after the sidecar was written, so every record
  claimed the reconstruction never finished. Now stamped once, before, and a
  test asserts the record agrees with the job.

Derivation is best-effort: a reconstruction that succeeded is never discarded
because a delivery format could not be produced.

37 server tests. Verified end-to-end against the contributor's real 9-frame
package, twice consecutively — the harness no longer assumes a clean data
directory, since a test that can only be run once is one people stop running.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
